The exception must either be uncaught (terminating the process, or at least the thread) or caught within the originating language's runtime (i.e. C++ exceptions must be caught in C++). It does not matter whether the function that _catches_ the exception is invoked with `"C"` or `"C-unwind"`, since those ABIs only have different behavior if an exception actually "escapes" through them.

